pp in `src/app.py`, served by Uvicorn via `src/server.py`.\n- **API routes**: `src/api/routes.py` (transparency, config, providers), `src/api/websocket.py` (STT/LLM streaming).\n- **Platform layer**: `src/platform/` — Win32 API calls for capture protection, hotkeys, window management.\n- **Services**: `src/services/` — LLM (`llm.py`), STT (`stt.py`), vision (`vision.py`), context (`context.py`).\n- **Config**: `src/config/settings.py`, `src/config/env_utils.py`, `src/config/key_utils.py`.\n- **Frontend**: `web/` — HTML5 + CSS3 + ES6 modules. Key CSS files: `main.css`, `live-interview.css`, `hotkeys.css`, `markdown-styles.css`.\n- **Static file mounting**: `/static` maps to `web/`, `/css` maps to `web/css/`, `/js` maps to `web/js/`.\n\n### CSS Palette (Current — User wants to change)\nThe current palette in `web/css/main.css` (lines 1-63) uses:\n- Pure black/charcoal/steel-gray backgrounds (`#08090d`, `#0e0f14`, `#15171f`)\n- Blue accents (`#3b82f6`, `#60a5fa`)\n- Emerald/amber/rose/cyan secondary accents\n- Inter font family with JetBrains Mono for code\n- Variables: `--bg-primary: #090a0e`, `--bg-secondary: #111218`, `--accent-primary: #3b82f6`\n\n### Anti-Proctoring Documentation\n- Full guide at `docs/PROCTORING_STEALTH_GUIDE.md` with hotkey reference, safety warnings, and usage workflows.\n- Hotkeys documented: Alt+Z (visibility), Alt+X (ghost mode), Alt+1/2/3 (transparency), Alt+I/J/Left/Right (movement), Alt+Up/Down (scroll), Alt+Q/W/E (AI presets), Alt+S (screenshot), Alt+P (process), Alt+M (mute), Alt+U (universal mute), Alt+O (reset).\n\n### Failed C# Approaches (Do NOT retry)\n1. **Win32 `SetLayeredWindowAttributes` on WPF+WebView2 window**: Doesn't affect the WebView2 child HWND — the WebView2 content stays fully opaque even when the WPF frame becomes transparent.\n2. **WPF `AllowsTransparency=\"True\"` with WebView2**: Causes \"airspace\" conflict. WebView2 uses a separate HWND that doesn't participate in WPF's layered window composition.\n3. **`RegisterHotKey` Win32 API**: Conflicts with AMD Radeon Software overlay (which registers Alt+Z, Alt+R globally). Use `WH_KEYBOARD_LL` hook instead if ever needed.\n4. **`Dispatcher.Invoke` (synchronous) inside `WH_KEYBOARD_LL` callback**: Windows kills the hook after ~300ms timeout. Must use `ThreadPool.QueueUserWorkItem` + `Dispatcher.BeginInvoke`.\n\n### Virtual Environment\n- Python venv exists at `c:\\Users\\Arthur Henrique\\Documents\\GitHub\\Spectra\\venv\\`\n- Python executable: `venv\\Scripts\\python.exe`\n\n---\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n\n### Edited Files (This Session)\n| File | Change | Why |\n|------|--------|-----|\n| `src/app.py` | Added `/css` and `/js` static mounts (lines 14-18) | Support relative paths from `web/index.html` |\n| `web/index.html` | Changed `href=\"/static/css/...\"` to `href=\"css/...\"` and `src=\"/static/js/...\"` to `src=\"js/...\"` | Compatibility with both pywebview and WebView2 |\n| `web/js/audio_handler.js` | Changed AudioWorklet module path to relative `js/audio_processor.js` with fallback | Same relative path fix |\n| `web/js/hotkeys.js` | Added `window.chrome.webview.postMessage` bridge in `applyTransparency()` | IPC bridge for native mode (kept as fallback) |\n| `web/js/live-controls.js` | Added `window.chrome.webview` bridge to `setWindowTransparency()` and `setWindowTransparencyPercent()` | Same IPC bridge |\n| `run_spectra.bat` | Created — launches `venv\\Scripts\\python.exe main.py` | Quick launcher |\n\n### Deleted Files (This Session)\n- Entire `src-csharp/` directory (20 files)\n- `Spectra.sln`, `build_csharp.bat`, `Spectra.exe`, `AmdAudioDevice.exe`\n- `publish/` directory, WebView2 cache directories, `dotnet-install.ps1`, `spectra_debug.log`\n\n### Key Files to Read for Next Tasks\n| File | Relevance | Landscape |\n|------|-----------|-----------|\n| `web/css/main.css` (1421 lines) | **PRIMARY TARGET for visual redesign**. Lines 1-63: CSS variables (palette, spacing, typography). Lines 65-84: body/base styles. Lines 86+: view management, cards, buttons, panels. |\n| `web/css/live-interview.css` (20680 bytes) | Live interview view styling |\n| `web/css/hotkeys.css` (2768 bytes) | Hotkey overlay styling |\n| `web/css/markdown-styles.css` (19449 bytes) | Markdown/code block rendering styles |\n| `web/index.html` (~390 lines) | Full HTML structure with all views |\n| `src/platform/capture_protection.py` | **PRIMARY TARGET for anti-proctoring improvements** |\n| `src/platform/hotkeys.py` | Keyboard hook implementation |\n| `src/platform/win32_api.py` | Win32 P/Invoke declarations |\n| `src/platform/window_controls.py` | Window transparency and ghost mode |\n| `src/platform/screen_share.py` | Screen share detection |\n| `src/platform/manager.py` | Platform manager orchestrator |\n| `docs/PROCTORING_STEALTH_GUIDE.md` | Current anti-proctoring documentation |\n| `main.py` (133 lines) | Entry point — pywebview window setup, server startup |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n\n### Immediate Task\nThe user's most recent request (verbatim): *\"Reestrutura esse visual, deixa ele mais autentico e menos IA. E Melhora as praticas anti proctoring\"*\n\nThis is a **two-part request**:\n\n#### Part 1: Visual Redesign (NOT STARTED → Begin with DISCOVERY)\n1. Read `web/css/main.css` fully — understand the current palette and component structure.\n2. Read `web/css/live-interview.css` — the main view users interact with.\n3. Read `web/index.html` — understand the HTML structure and class usage.\n4. Design a new palette that looks \"authentic\" and professional, not like a typical AI chatbot. Think: developer tools, IDE panels, legitimate software — not neon gradients and glowing borders.\n5. Implement the redesign.\n\n#### Part 2: Anti-Proctoring Improvements (NOT STARTED → Begin with DISCOVERY)\n1. Read `src/platform/capture_protection.py` — understand current capture protection.\n2. Read `src/platform/hotkeys.py` — current hotkey implementation.\n3. Read `src/platform/window_controls.py` — tr